Agent: Tropical Pineapple–Mango Punch (non‑alcoholic) — serves ~12

Ingredients:
- 8 cups (64 fl oz) pineapple juice
- 4 cups (32 fl oz) mango nectar or mango puree diluted to drinking consistency
- 2 cups (16 fl oz) orange juice
- 1 cup (8 fl oz) passion fruit juice (or passion fruit concentrate diluted)
- 1/2 cup fresh lime juice
- 1/4 cup grenadine (for color and a touch of sweetness)
- 2 liters chilled ginger ale (or club soda for less sweetness)
- 3 cups frozen pineapple and mango chunks (acts as ice)
- Fresh mint sprigs and thin orange/lime slices for garnish

Instructions:
1. Chill all juices ahead of time.
2. In a large punch bowl or beverage dispenser, combine pineapple juice, mango nectar, orange juice, passion fruit juice, lime juice, and grenadine. Stir to mix.
3. Add the frozen fruit chunks to the bowl (they keep the punch cold without diluting it quickly).
4. Just before serving, slowly add the chilled ginger ale and gently stir to combine.
5. Garnish with mint sprigs and citrus slices. Serve over additional ice if desired.

Make-ahead tip: Mix the juices (everything except ginger ale and frozen fruit) up to 24 hours ahead and refrigerate. Add ginger ale and frozen fruit right before serving for best fizz and chill.
